<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalmar War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1611">1611</a>–<a href="/years/1613">1613</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar">Kalmar</a> War was fought between Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1611 to 1613. Christian IV attacked to assert Danish dominance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> and to stop Swedish expansion in the Arctic north. Danish forces took Kalmar and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvsborg">Älvsborg</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-knared">Treaty of Knäred</a> forced Sweden to pay a large ransom for Älvsborg, its only outlet to the west. It was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>'s last clear victory over Sweden.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalmar-war.jpg" alt="Kalmar War" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LocalF15 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalmar_War_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
